A||||10||K9||Idle problem???||||
Z||000000||K9||09-05-99||06:12 PM||||My 85 GT Has a smal iratic idleing problem. While the car is in "P"or"N" the idle goes up and down about 200rpm. There are no vacquam leaks and all tune up parts are new. It seems like a lot of peole have this problem, is there a common fix. Could the idle air control valve be the problem.Is so where is it and how do i fix it. Thanks for the help.
Z||000001||theogre||09-05-99||08:29 PM||||Idle floating is common in EFI cars of all types. if it's only 200 RPM it's about normal in most everything I've seen. Even in my own car, depending on conditions at the time, it floats one time and not the next.<p>Allot of it has to do with the ECM trying to Idle the car as low as it posibly can. There's a whole bunch of things that can affect it. You could replace parts till hell freezes and not get it to stop.
Z||000002||88 Fiero||09-05-99||09:50 PM||||try and clean out your IAC...go to your local auto parts and buy the Berryman Chemtool B-12 throttle body cleaner...pull the IAC out and with a rag spary the chem tool cleaner...wipe  it around the pintle of the IAC...be careful when you do this...also push the pintle back...now put a lot of rags underneat the throttle body and spray the inside of the throttle body...again..spray the rag and open the butterfly and try and clean as much as you can...also the hole where you screw the IAC spray it with the solution and clean it out with a rag...be sure it's all dry before you put the IAC back in...this should help...
Z||000003||K9||09-06-99||07:14 AM||||88 Fiero thanks for the info. I dont now what an IAC is or where it is located or even what it looks like.
Z||000004||88 Fiero||09-06-99||07:50 AM||||if you opened your deck lid and looking at the throttle body you will notice there are 2 sensors that are hook on the side...one is kinda on the middle and kinda flat looking and wires at the back end...and the other one is below kinda round and wires at the end...the one below is the IAC...first disconnect the connector..be careful not to break the lock part of it...then use a wrench and unscrew that IAC...look at it and I will guarantee you that it's dirty..black dirt in it...just clean it the way I've instructed...pushed that pintle back....slowly....it's the cone shape of the IAC 
Z||000005||mwbackus||09-06-99||11:02 AM||||The IAC is simply a stepper motor operating a valve.  One of the problems inherent with this type of device is that the response time will deteriorate with age.  This condition will usually not set a trouble code, but will effect idle and performance significantly.  A clean seat surface is very important and the information above is exactly what I would advise to keep a "good" IAC operating as intended, however, a replacement would be in order if the age or actual condition of the IAC is unknown.  One should pay close attention to the condition of the gasket, it is very common for a leak to occur here.  I would also suggest using thread locking compound (permatex "red" or equiv.) upon reinstallation.<p>Mike<br>88 Formula (108k)
Z||000006||AL||09-06-99||10:05 PM||||just buy brake cleaner, one can.break cleaner cleans best an it desolves anything fast, and the best part is that it dries quick. check the measurement on your valve. clean the throtle also and the plate inside, trust me it works real good.
Z||000007||K9||09-06-99||11:56 PM||||Well I tried to do what all you helpfull fiero lovers said...Remove the IAC and clean it and inside of the intake.I couldent get the IAC unscrewed. I tried the Common tools but couldent get it off as the fuil line is in the way. So all I did was remove the intake pipe and cleaned the inside withsome Holly intake/carb cleaner.This has helped the problem but has not fixed it. 
Z||000008||4Banger Bandit||09-08-1999||01:33 AM||||I tried the same damn thing, and had the same problem.  I think those are coolant lines aren't they?  In any case, they are in the way, and I don't see any other way to removed the IAC.  Did you guys remove these lines??? My car has the very same idle problem.||||reg||
Z||000009||AL||09-08-1999||06:32 AM||||IT'S EASY TO REMOVE, TRY A GOOD OLD MONKEY WRENCH, IF YOU STILL CAN'T GET AT IT GET SOME PLIERS, THE ONES THAT HAVE AN ANGLE TO THEM. AND LAST TRY A SMALL VICE GRIP IT TAKES A LITTLE TIME BUT IT WORKS.||||reg||
Z||000010||AL||09-08-1999||06:37 AM||||IT'S EASY TO REMOVE, TRY A GOOD OLD <BR>MONKEY WRENCH, IF YOU STILL CAN'T GET AT <BR>IT GET SOME PLIERS, THE ONES THAT HAVE AN <BR>ANGLE TO THEM. AND LAST TRY A SMALL VICE <BR>GRIP IT TAKES A LITTLE TIME BUT IT WORKS.I FORGOT TO MENTION DON'T PUT ANY LOCK TREAD SEALANT ON IT,BECAUSE IF YOU WANT TO CLEAN IT AGAIN,YOU WILL HAVE A HARDER TIME TO REMOVE IT.||||reg||
